The Project: WalletWatcher 💸
Unlike the Todo app (which was just one table), this app will have two tables linked together. This will force you to practice Prisma Relations, which is a key backend skill.

The Data Model (Schema)
    Category: (e.g., "Food", "Travel", "Bills")
        id: Int
        name: String
    Expense: (e.g., "Uber to Airport", $45.00)
        id: Int
        title: String
        amount: Float
        date: DateTime
        categoryId: Int (Foreign Key linking to Category)

Phase 1: Local Setup (The Foundation)
    [done] Initialize project - npm init & TypeScript setup (tsconfig.json).(npm init, tsc --init, install express, pg, dotenv).
    [done] Express Server running on port 3000.
    [done] Create docker-compose.yml immediately to spin up a local PostgreSQL container.
    [done] Connect to the DB using a tool (like DBeaver or VS Code SQLTools) to verify it's running.
        
Phase 1.1: The Manual Connection Pool
    [done] Create a file src/db/pool.ts.
    [done] Configure the Pool class explicitly (host, user, password, port).
    [done] Critical Task: Set max: 10 (or similar) to explicitly define your pool size.
    [done] Export a query function that uses this pool.

Phase 2: The Logic (CRUD)
